From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: CoreXGT <aulia.ikbal09@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 21:42:00 +0700
Subject: [PATCH] sepolicy: allow init to swapon zram0 (nikel zRAM swap)

cm-13.0 port of the cm-14.1 patch of the same name.

init.zram.rc (device tree) sets /sys/block/zram0/disksize and runs
mkswap+swapon on /dev/block/zram0, which carries the ram_device label.
Give init rw_file_perms on it; the disksize write is already covered by
the existing "allow init sysfs_type:file w_file_perms".

cm-13.0 keeps the policy in external/sepolicy (not system/sepolicy), and
its init.te has no ram_device rule yet.

Change-Id: I0000000000000000000000000000000000000005
---
 init.te | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/init.te b/init.te
--- a/init.te
+++ b/init.te
@@ -156,5 +156,9 @@
 # Write to sysfs nodes.
 allow init sysfs_type:dir r_dir_perms;
 allow init sysfs_type:file w_file_perms;
+
+# nikel zRAM swap: mkswap + swapon /dev/block/zram0 (device tree nikel
+# init.zram.rc). /dev/block/ram* carries the ram_device label.
+allow init ram_device:blk_file rw_file_perms;
 
 # Transitions to seclabel processes in init.rc
--
2.53.0
